// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  38 — Persistent Constants (const const const)                ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
//
// A triple-const declaration stores an immutable value that PERSISTS
// across separate runs of the program (saved to disk by the runtime).

// Declare persistent constants:
const const const APP_NAME = "Gulf of Mexico"!
const const const VERSION = "1.0"!

print APP_NAME!
print VERSION!

// They behave like ordinary immutable constants within the program:
print "${APP_NAME} v${VERSION}"!

// Because they persist, the first run "seeds" them; later runs reuse the
// stored value. (Remove the runtime's persistence directory to reset.)
